Both OData V2 and V4 receiver adapters in SAP CPI facilitate integration with OData services. However,
OData V4 is the recommended choice for new developments due to its enhanced performance, data handling,
and future readiness.

Key Differences
✅ 1. Metadata Handling
V2: Transmits metadata in a verbose format.
V4: Utilizes a compressed and optimized metadata format, reducing payload size and improving retrieval performance.

✅ 2. Data Types
V2: Uses broader data types.
V4: Supports more granular types (e.g., separate Date and Time types), improving precision and query flexibility.

✅ 3. Query Capabilities
V2: Limited filtering, especially on expanded entities.
V4: Supports advanced filtering, sorting, and querying on nested/expanded entities
(e.g., filter order items while expanding order headers).

✅ 4. Error Handling
V2: Provides basic error messages.
V4: Returns detailed and structured error responses, aiding in faster and more accurate troubleshooting.

✅ 5. HTTP Methods
V2: Uses MERGE along with the X-HTTP-METHOD header.
V4: Leverages the PATCH method for partial updates, aligning better with modern RESTful practices.

✅ 6. Batch Processing
Both: Support $batch processing.
V4: Provides improved handling of multiple operations in a single call with better error segregation.

✅ 7. Annotations
V4: Makes extensive use of OData annotations, offering better integration with tools like SAP Fiori Elements and UI5.

Benefits of OData V4
🔹 Improved Performance: Smaller metadata and response payloads boost speed and responsiveness.
🔹 Data Efficiency: Enhanced query capabilities reduce data volume and improve transmission efficiency.
🔹 Modern Standards: Aligns with current RESTful principles and is better supported by modern development tools.
🔹 Future-Proofing: SAP and many third-party platforms are focusing more on V4, ensuring long-term support and compatibility.

